Spec: Boolean Operations

Purpose:
  Combine two or more shapes using set operations (unite, subtract, intersect, exclude).

Owns:
  ./boolean.ts

Can read:
  ../../core/math/boolean.ts

Must:
  Support four operations: unite, subtract, intersect, exclude.
  Require at least 2 selected shapes.
  Preserve z-order position (insert result at lowest original index).
  Remove original shapes and replace with result.
  Notify user when operation produces no result.
  Be fully undoable (restore originals on undo).

Must not:
  Modify shapes that are not selected.
  Silently fail without user feedback.
  Operate on text or group shapes directly (must be paths).

Depends on:
  paper.js (via @BooleanOperations)
  @useStore
  @notify

Scenario: unite two overlapping rectangles
  Given two overlapping rectangles are selected
  When the user clicks "Unite"
  Then a single merged shape replaces both rectangles
  And the result is selected

Scenario: no overlap produces warning
  Given two non-overlapping shapes are selected
  When the user clicks "Subtract"
  Then a warning notification appears
  And original shapes are preserved

Tasks:
  [x] Unite operation.
  [x] Subtract operation.
  [x] Intersect operation.
  [x] Exclude operation.
  [x] User notification on empty result.
  [x] Undo restores original shapes.
